Z||000010||My7Fieros||01-26-2001||01:05 PM||||<B>DROOL!!!!!!!!!!!</B> Both you guys seats look great! Hey, speaking of removing the old material, can you do it w/o tearing it? The seats in my SE are damn near mint, and I dont wont to ruin the fabric...can I take them off and not mess them up when installing the leather?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||BAM-BAM||01-26-2001||10:51 PM||||  M7, You don't have to tear up the old seat covers. If you are careful and follow the directions that Mr. Mike gives, all you have to  do is roll it up and pull it over the headrest. It's that simple. It took me all of 2 hours to do both seats. I took a little extra time and cleaned and recoated the seat rails with 316 stainless paint. It turned out GREAT!!. Good luck.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
